                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "32bfab44-c74f-343c-baa9-fb66f9a01afc",
                        "entry_id": "f83eb188-e68e-35f9-aee8-c44608efdbac",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Worthless finery; bric-a-brac or junk."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9af58e5a-8960-4c33-9ae6-1cb4c7758d8c",
                                "sense_id": "32bfab44-c74f-343c-baa9-fb66f9a01afc",
                                "text": "I have ſold all my Tromperie: not a counterfeit Stone, not a Ribbon, Glaſſe, Pomander, Browch, Table-booke, Ballad, Knife, Tape, Gloue, Shooe-tye, Bracelet, Horne-Ring, to keepe my Pack from faſting: […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c3669e37-f549-4a70-acc4-b8f54029e8d2",
                                "sense_id": "32bfab44-c74f-343c-baa9-fb66f9a01afc",
                                "text": "PROSPERO.^([To Ariel]) / This was well done, my bird. / Thy shape invisible retain thou still: / The trumpery in my house, go bring it hither / For stale to catch these thieves."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "04670a97-0696-362d-8c06-466580baa9b4",
                        "entry_id": "f83eb188-e68e-35f9-aee8-c44608efdbac",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Nonsense."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c9bad9d1-a401-4baa-b3ae-9f76e7440e6e",
                                "sense_id": "04670a97-0696-362d-8c06-466580baa9b4",
                                "text": "Now upon the coming of Chriſt, very much, tho' not all, of this idolatrous Trumpery and Superſtition was driven out of the World: […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8a7d6ede-2c53-3089-8433-8ef05dc1cd62",
                        "entry_id": "f83eb188-e68e-35f9-aee8-c44608efdbac",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Deceit; fraud."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "obsolete"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7e9ddf8a-1bf3-422a-8b9a-7c14fa055ab4",
                                "sense_id": "8a7d6ede-2c53-3089-8433-8ef05dc1cd62",
                                "text": "1640, Richard Greenwey, The Annales of Cornelius Tacitus. The Description of Germanie, publ. by Richard Whitaker, 182.\nAgrippina after this, more mad and wilfull then ever, gave out threatning and thundring ſpeeches: yet not forbearing the Princes eares, but crying, that Britannicus was now growen to mans eſtate : a true and worthy plant to receive his fathers Empire, which a grafted ſon by adoption now poſſeſſed by the injury and trumpery of his mother."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2903c96c-619f-452a-b0e4-ae467ef45f94",
                                "sense_id": "8a7d6ede-2c53-3089-8433-8ef05dc1cd62",
                                "text": "In that case there is no need for me to write about the trumpery scandal by which I was the sufferer—the innocent sufferer, I positively assert."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "bfb706e8-1749-48ab-8021-d14d5af2ddbc",
                        "source_entry_id": "f83eb188-e68e-35f9-aee8-c44608efdbac",
